[88.848837, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe install exceeded the command timeout because PyPI’s ARM Torch wheel pulls in a large CUDA stack. I’ll run a CPU-only install in the background and poll its \r\nlog.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app && nohup pip install --no-cache-dir --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu torch > /app/pip_torch.log 2>&1 & echo $! > /app/pip_torch.pid; cat\r\n/app/pip_torch.pid; sleep 2; tail -20 /app/pip_torch.log\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠙\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
