[229.222657, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe merge completed successfully and all 10 predictions map to the adapter’s expected language IDs with high confidence. I’ll now validate the on-disk \r\nartifacts, reload the merged model independently, and compare its predictions against the pre-merge adapter model to catch any serialization/merge issue.\r\n\r\n```\r\necho '--- model_cache'; find /app/model_cache/xlm-roberta-base -maxdepth 1 -type f -printf '%f %s\\n' | sort; echo '--- merged_model'; find /app/merged_model \r\n-maxdepth 1 -type f -printf '%f %s\\n' | sort; echo '--- detection_results.json'; cat /app/detection_results.json; echo; echo '--- configs'; python - <<'PY'\r\nimport json\r\nfor p in ['/app/model_cache/xlm-roberta-base/config.json','/app/merged_model/config.json']:\r\n    c=json.load(open(p))\r\n    print(p)\r\n    print(' architectures:',c.get('architectures'))\r\n    print(' num_labels:',c.get('num_labels'))\r\n    print(' id2label:',c.get('id2label'))\r\n    print(' label2id:',c.get('label2id'))\r\nPY\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond."]
[229.222666, "o", ".."]
